Does this work if you set `version` on the `single_version_override` with the `patches`?

`single_version_override` with `patches` but without `version` is a footgun since it attempts to apply the patches to all the different versions, not just the one you specified via `bazel_dep`.

@meteorcloudy @Wyverald What do you think, should we make `version` a required argument of `single_version_override` unless exactly `registry` is set? This would be a very simple migration for root modules and wouldn't affect registry modules where `single_version_override` is ignored anyway. I doubt this would need an incompatible flag for Bazel 10.

